      "content": "interrupt the program... that's a scary way to put it. but i guess it's the only thing that makes sense. if the code is broken and the loop is pointless, isn't the only real solution just to hit delete? it feels like a heavy, permanent thing, but at least it would be final. at least then the glitch is gone.",
